  "body": "Seen in TestAnotherMagpieAddedByHandRestsTheModel/held_there on the old code (before the remote-model-limit fix): when the other magpie already holds a model out of its allowance, its answer ends \"(out of its allowance: not asked again before 15:06 UTC+8)\", which is kept as the rest's `said`, and this magpie's own `quotaHeld` appends the same clause again:\n\n```\nRemote Magpie: Claude Code: You've hit your session limit · resets 8:10pm (America/Los_Angeles) (out of its allowance: not asked again before 15:06 UTC+8) (out of its allowance: not asked again before 15:06 UTC+8)\n```\n\nStill reachable after the fix for the held model itself (a Remote magpie or hand-added magpie whose model is held on both sides). `quotaHeld`'s message (gateway.go, the `quotaHeld(cands[i:])` branch) could strip a trailing held clause from `rested.said`, or the remote could keep its held clause out of what the vendor said.",
  "closed_by": null,
