   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3701-held-clause` (head `5253cad3`, on upstream `6afbe3f3`) — a held refusal relayed from another magpie says its clause once.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/gateway/gateway.go`'s held branch (`quotaHeld`) formats `\"%s (out of its allowance: not asked again before %s)\"` around `rested.said`. When the refusing upstream is another magpie, `rested.said` is already that sentence with the clause in it, so the clause lands twice. It is the only place that builds this clause (`heldClock`'s other users say \"until …\").\n\n**Change.** strip a trailing clause from `rested.said` before formatting (a `heldSaid` helper that cuts at the stable `\" (out of its allowance: \"` prefix), so the refusal says it once whether it was written here or relayed.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/ -run TestRemoteMagpieHeldRefusalSaysItsClauseOnce` → `remote_magpie_key_limit_test.go:248: the held refusal says the clause 2 times: 429 {… (out of its allowance: not asked again before 05:32 UTC+10) (out of its allowance: …)}`\nGreen: `same command → `ok`; the refusal asked there and the one held here each say it once` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gateway`\n\nThe test runs the two-gateway harness the file already builds (a real inner magpie served over httptest), so the relay path is the reported one, not a mock.\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 26's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6afbe3f3` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3701-held-clause — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
